{"step_index":146,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T19:08:00Z","content":"# AUTOMIND AI — Phase 1 Initialization Complete\n\nThe foundational architecture for **AUTOMIND AI** has been established at:\n`C:\\Users\\chauh\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\automind-ai`\n\n*(Recommendation: Set `automind-ai` as your active workspace folder in your IDE).*\n\n---\n\n### What Was Created\n\n#### 1. Architecture Blueprint & Monorepo Structure\n* **[README.md](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/README.md)**: End-to-end system architecture specification, REST API contracts, data flows, security boundaries, and local startup workflows.\n* **[package.json](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/package.json)** & **[.gitignore](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/.gitignore)**: Root workspace commands and repository hygiene rules.\n\n#### 2. Frontend Layer (`frontend/`)\n* **Framework**: Next.js (App Router), React 18, TypeScript (Strict), Tailwind CSS, Framer Motion, Three.js, React Three Fiber (`@react-three/fiber`, `@react-three/drei`), Lucide React.\n* **Base Design System (Luxury Dark Automotive Theme)**:\n  * **[globals.css](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/frontend/app/globals.css)** & **[tailwind.config.ts](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/frontend/tailwind.config.ts)**: Obsidian backgrounds (`#07090E`), cyber cyan glow (`#00F0FF`), crimson accents (`#FF2A54`), custom glassmorphism (`backdrop-blur-md`), and carbon grid lines.\n  * **Reusable Atomic Components**:\n    * [`Button`](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/frontend/components/ui/button.tsx) (variants: `primary`, `secondary`, `crimson`, `outline`, `ghost`, `glass` with loading states)\n    * [`Card`](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/frontend/components/ui/card.tsx) (glassmorphism panels with optional neon glow)\n    * [`Badge`](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/frontend/components/ui/badge.tsx) (high-contrast automotive status indicators)\n \n<truncated 1766 bytes>\n/session.py): Supabase connection management.\n* **Decoupled Services & Schemas**:\n  * [`app/services/ai_service.py`](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/backend/app/services/ai_service.py): Google Gemini integration for assistant chat and recommendation reasoning.\n  * [`app/services/ml_service.py`](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/backend/app/services/ml_service.py): ML model loader and feature impact breakdown.\n  * [`app/services/car_service.py`](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/backend/app/services/car_service.py): Vehicle catalog and comparison service.\n* **Versioned Endpoints (`/api/v1/`)**:\n  * `/health`, `/cars`, `/ml/predict-price`, `/ai/chat`, `/ai/recommend`.\n\n#### 4. Machine Learning Subsystem (`ml/`)\n* **[ml/README.md](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/ml/README.md)**: ML pipeline documentation and training lifecycle.\n* **[ml/src/data_pipeline.py](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/ml/src/data_pipeline.py)**: Scikit-learn `ColumnTransformer` with `OneHotEncoder`, `StandardScaler`, and median imputers.\n* **[ml/src/train.py](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/ml/src/train.py)**: XGBoost Regressor training pipeline evaluating RMSE, MAE, and $R^2$.\n* **[ml/src/predict.py](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/ml/src/predict.py)**: Inference wrapper for production model serving.\n\n---\n\n### Verification Summary\n- **Frontend Dependencies**: Installed cleanly.\n- **TypeScript**: `npx tsc --noEmit` verified with 0 errors.\n- **Next.js Production Build**: `npm run build` compiled and optimized successfully.\n- **Python Backend & ML Code**: Compiled and syntax-validated with `py_compile`.\n\nThe full report is available in the [Walkthrough Artifact](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/brain/10f22c6a-7cf9-4af6-ab9e-ed172ecaddf1/walkthrough.md).\n\nI have stopped as instructed. What would you like to build or connect next?","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":147,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T19:13:11Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nNow build the visual design system for AutoMind AI.\r\n\r\nDesign direction:\r\n\r\nPremium futuristic automotive website.\r\n\r\nVisual characteristics:\r\n\r\n* cinematic\r\n* minimal\r\n* luxurious\r\n* futuristic\r\n* sophisticated\r\n* dark\r\n* high contrast\r\n* subtle glass effects\r\n* smooth micro-interactions\r\n\r\nCreate:\r\n\r\n1. Global typography\r\n2. Color tokens\r\n3. Spacing system\r\n4. Border radius system\r\n5. Buttons\r\n6. Cards\r\n7. Inputs\r\n8. Badges\r\n9. Section containers\r\n10. Loading states\r\n11. Error states\r\n\r\nUse a restrained visual system.\r\n\r\nDo not overuse gradients, glassmorphism or animations.\r\n\r\nUse Framer Motion for reusable animation utilities.\r\n\r\nCreate reusable components instead of duplicating styles.\r\n\r\nDo not create the complete pages yet.\r\n\r\nAfter implementation, run the application and verify that there are no build errors.\r\n\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-01T00:43:11+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":148,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T19:13:11Z","thinking":"Initial assessment of the user's request reveals the need for a visual design system, specifically for an automotive AI website. Design characteristics emphasize a premium, futuristic aesthetic; cinematic and minimal qualities seem key. Global typography needs to reflect this direction, with an emphasis on cinematic headings and a clean mono typeface.\n\n\nInitial color palette consideration includes deep obsidian, titanium, graphite, and subtle electric cyan or ice blue for accents, alongside champagne gold or amber, and crimson accents. A balanced spacing system, combined with precision automotive angles for border radii (sleek curves and sharp corners), will support the desired aesthetic. Reusable components like buttons (with Framer Motion interactions), cards (minimal obsidian, frosted glass), and inputs (crisp focus rings) are prioritized.\n\nBadges, section containers, loading states (skeleton loaders, radar spinners), and error states (empty states with retry buttons) need careful design to maintain visual consistency. Animation utilities will be handled via Framer Motion, focusing on reusable animation wrappers. The approach avoids excessive gradients, glassmorphism, or complex animations, focusing instead on a restrained visual system.\n\n\nAn implementation plan is required due to the scope of the design system: typography, color tokens, animations, atomic UI components, and page demo. Existing file inspection confirms the project's structure, including existing components and theme configuration. The visual design system architecture will focus on tokens and theme configuration, defining a refined color palette within a `theme.ts` file.\n\n\nA preliminary color palette is defined, encompassing dark obsidian, muted gray, ice cyan, metallic titanium, warm gold, and a vibrant crimson. Examination of the project structure reveals existing animation wrappers, typography scales, border-radius tokens, and subtle gradient configurations within the framework.\n\nReusable UI components are being refined, including specialized typography elements for headings, text, and technical labels. Button components will use micro-interactions and support variants with diverse styles. Card components are tailored for minimal obsidian, frosted glass, and technical specification displays.\n\n\nInitial component inventory suggests a focused design system with specific automotive UI elements. The plan should detail the creation and integration of input controls, selection menus, sliders, switches, and status badges. Section containers, loading states, and alert components are essential for a robust user experience.\n\nAn interactive showcase will serve to demonstrate each element's functionality and visual style. The showcase needs a cinematic, dark layout to present all UI elements with micro-interactions, allowing for interactive testing of the implemented components. The `implementation_plan.md` artifact will be structured to address component design, implementation, and integration.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":true,\"Summary\":\"Implementation plan for the AutoMind AI Visual Design System (typography, colors, spacing, radius, buttons, cards, inputs, badges, containers, loading and error states with Framer Motion).\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# AutoMind AI — Visual Design System Implementation Plan\\n\\n## Design Direction & Philosophy\\n**AutoMind AI** embodies a **cinematic, minimal, luxurious, futuristic, and dark** automotive design aesthetic:\\n- **Restraint Over Excess**: Sharp typography, crisp alpha borders (`rgba(255,255,255,0.06)`), obsidian depth, and calculated neon accents rather than noisy gradients or aggressive blur effects.\\n- **Precision & Telemetry**: Technical eyebrows (`// 01 ARCHITECTURE`), geometric metric displays, and high-contrast status chips.\\n- **Tactile Micro-Interactions**: Fluid Framer Motion physics (spring-based tap reactions, subtle hover lifts, smooth state transitions).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## User Review Required\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> The design system avoids bloated external UI libraries (like shadcn copy-pastes with unused Radix primitives) in favor of high-performance, lightweight, custom-crafted TypeScript + Tailwind + Framer Motion components tailored specifically for automotive visualization and telemetry.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Proposed System Structure & Changes\\n\\n### 1. Foundations & Tokens\\n- [MODIFY] [`frontend/lib/constants/theme.ts`](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/frontend/lib/constants/theme.ts) — Refined color tokens: Obsidian `#06080C`, Carbon `#0B0F17`, Steel `#141B29`, Cyber Cyan `#00F0FF`, Champagne Gold `#D4AF37`, Hyper Crimson `#FF2A54`, Emerald `#10B981`, and border opacity scales.\\n- [NEW] [`frontend/lib/motion.ts`](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/frontend/lib/motion.ts) — Reusable Framer Motion transitions, spring configurations, hover physics, stagger containers, and fade variants.\\n- [MODIFY] [`frontend/tailwind.config.ts`](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/automind-ai/frontend/tailwind.config.ts) — Extended border-radius system (`xs: 4px`, `sm: 6px`, `md: 10px`, `lg: 14px`, `xl: 20px`), letter-spacing tokens, and subtle backdrop filters.\\n- [MODIFY] [`frontend/app/globals.css`](file:///C:/Users/chauh/.gemini/antigravity/scra\n<truncated 4141 bytes>","Description":"\"Create implementation plan for the AutoMind AI visual design system\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chauh\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\10f22c6a-7cf9-4af6-ab9e-ed172ecaddf1\\\\implementation_plan.md\"","toolAction":"\"Creating design system plan\"","toolSummary":"\"Create implementation_plan.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
